   "definition_quote": "In the latter, each triple $(x_t, m_t, \\ell_t)$ is drawn independently from a fixed and unknown distribution $\\calD$.\n\nAs in the standard contextual bandits setup, the learner has access to some fixed policy class $\\Pi \\subseteq [K]^\\calX$, assumed to be finite (for simplicity) with cardinality $N$, and her goal is to minimize the (pseudo) regret against the best fixed policy:\n$$\n  \\textstyle  \\Reg(\\calA) \\triangleq \\max_{\\pi\\in\\Pi} \\E\\big[\\sum_{t=1}^T \\ell_t(a_t) - \\sum_{t=1}^T \\ell_t(\\pi(x_t))\\big],\n$$\nwhere the expectation is with respect to the randomness of the learner, denoted as the algorithm $\\calA$ which chooses $a_1, \\ldots, a_T$, and also that of the environment in the stochastic case."
  },
